        "Zürich Tourismo www.zuerich.com"@it ;
    schema:dateModified "2025-11-26T04:35:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:description "<p>Die Destination Z&uuml;rich erh&auml;lt eines ihrer Wahrzeichen zur&uuml;ck. Die glanzvolle Vergangenheit und lebendige Zukunft des traditionsreichen Hauses gehen eine spannende Symbiose ein, die sich in der Architektur von Foster and Partners, im Innendesign von United Designers sowie im Spa-Konzept von Sylvia Sepielli widerspiegelt. Augenf&auml;llig wird diese auf den ersten Blick in den k&uuml;hnen Erweiterungs- und Umbauten der renommierten englischen Architekten Foster and Partners. Sie restaurierten die Fassade des historischen Hauptgeb&auml;udes in seinen Ursprungszustand von 1899 und f&uuml;gten zwei spektakul&auml;re, geschwungene Fl&uuml;gelbauten hinzu: 175 luxuri&ouml;se Zimmer und Suiten, einen Spa-Bereich auf 4'000 Quadratmetern, erlesene Gastronomie sowie grossz&uuml;gige Bankett- und Seminarr&auml;umlichkeiten.</p>"@de,
        "<p>The tradition-steeped hotel, The Dolder Grand &ndash; which first opened in 1899 as the Dolder Grand Hotel &amp; Curhaus &ndash; lies on the idyllic Z&uuml;richberg, offering a magnificent view out over the city, Lake Zurich, and the Alps. A total of 175 luxurious rooms and suites invite guests to switch off and chill out, while a 4,000 m2 (43,000 sq.ft.) <a href=\"https://www.zuerich.com/en/node/1946\">large spa</a> promises pure relaxation in highly exclusive surroundings. Spacious rooms are available for special events, providing a stylish setting for any occasion.<p>The Dolder Grand also houses an impressive art collection comprising over 100 works by world-famous artists, such as Takashi Murakami and Salvador Dal&iacute;, which take guests on an inspiring journey through the world of art.</p><p>Four restaurants, seasonal pop-ups, a gourmet festival, and the Canvas Bar &amp; Lounge make the drinking and dining culture at the Dolder Grand a very special experience:</p><p>Awaiting hungry guests in the <a href=\"https://www.zuerich.com/node/88672\">Saltz </a>restaurant with bar (15 GaultMillau points) is a modern kitchen serving a wide selection of choice wines. Lovers of fine dining, meanwhile, are treated to culinary masterpieces at <a href=\"https://www.zuerich.com/en/node/3688\">The Restaurant</a> (2 Michelin stars, 19 GaultMillau points), with its exquisite, innovative gourmet cuisine. At the Restaurant&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.zuerich.com/en/visit/restaurants/mikuriya\">MIKURIYA</a>&nbsp;(16 GaultMillau points), guests enjoy a unique Omakase experience. The culinary offering is further complemented by the outstanding garden restaurant, &ldquo;<a href=\"https://www.zuerich.com/node/1011875\" data-entity-uuid=\"8b27304b-bcd3-470e-ac52-27a9ecc24904\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\">Blooms</a>&rdquo; (15 GaultMillau points).</p><p>The hotel&rsquo;s spacious terraces not only offer spectacular views of the city, Lake Zurich and the Alps, but also invite guests to relax and linger awhile.&nbsp;</p><p>The city center can be reached quickly and easily: with the free shuttle service, the nearby Dolderbahn funicular, or the limousine service, which can be ordered on request.</p></p>"@en,
        "<p>Apr&egrave;s une phase de construction de quatre ans, Zurich c&eacute;l&egrave;bre le retour de l&rsquo;un de ses monuments les plus en vue. Le \"Curhaus\" (centre thermal), construit en 1899, a &eacute;t&eacute; transform&eacute; en un complexe urbain de luxe. En m&ecirc;me temps, le pass&eacute; &eacute;tincelant et l'avenir vibrant de l'h&ocirc;tel ont &eacute;t&eacute; fusionn&eacute;s, comme en t&eacute;moignent l'architecture de Foster and Partners, le design int&eacute;rieur de United Designers et le concept de spa de Sylvia Sepielli. Cela est &eacute;vident d&egrave;s l'instant o&ugrave; vous voyez les lignes audacieuses de l'extension et de la conversion r&eacute;alis&eacute;es par les architectes r&eacute;put&eacute;s Foster and Partners. Ils ont restaur&eacute; la fa&ccedil;ade de l'ancien b&acirc;timent principal dans son &eacute;tat d'origine de 1899 et y ont ajout&eacute; deux ailes spectaculaires: 175 chambres et suites luxueuses, un spa de 4 000 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s, une cuisine de premi&egrave;re classe et des salles de banquets et de s&eacute;minaires aux proportions g&eacute;n&eacute;reuses.</p>"@fr,
        "<p>Dopo una fase di costruzione della durata di quattro anni, Zurigo celebra il ritorno di uno dei suoi monumenti pi&ugrave; importanti. L'originale \"Curhaus\" (centro benessere), costruito nel 1899, &egrave; stato trasformato in un resort di lusso di classe. Nel processo, il passato scintillante e il vibrante futuro dell'hotel sono stati fusi insieme, come riflesso nell'architettura di Foster and Partners, l'interior design di United Designers e il concetto di spa di Sylvia Sepielli. Questo &egrave; ovvio nel momento in cui vedi le linee audaci dell'estensione e della conversione eseguite dai noti architetti Foster and Partners. Hanno restaurato la facciata dello storico edificio principale nel suo stato originale del 1899 e aggiunto due spettacolari ali: 175 lussuose camere e suite, una spa di circa 4.000 metri quadrati, una cucina di prima classe e spazi per banchetti e seminari generosamente proporzionati.</p>"@it ;
    schema:disambiguatingDescription "Seit über 100 Jahren bietet das The Dolder Grand luxuriöse Hoteltradition an exklusiver Lage über den Dächern von Zürich."@de,
        "For over a century, The Dolder Grand has offered luxury hospitality in an exclusive location, high above the rooftops of Zurich."@en,
        "Depuis plus d’un siècle, The Dolder Grand qui bénéficie d’une situation exclusive sur les toits de Zurich peut se targuer d’avoir su conserver sa tradition hôtelière et son luxe."@fr,
        "Da oltre 100 anni, il The Dolder Grand propone la sua lussuosa tradizione alberghiera in posizione esclusiva sopra i tetti di Zurigo."@it ;
    schema:email "info@thedoldergrand.com" ;
    schema:geo _:N082a8c7ac28241d1ad1193617f2ae3a7 ;
