    schema:dateModified "2026-02-10T17:46:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:description "<p>Leidglich zwei Zutaten brauchen die Macher/-innen von Gar&ccedil;oa, um ihre intensive Schokolade zu produzieren. Das klingt einfach, bedingt allerdings die allerbesten Zutaten &ndash; sprich reinsten Kakao und besten Rohrzucker &ndash; sowie Zeit.<p>Bei der Bean-to-Bar-Bewegung &uuml;berwachen Produzenten jeden Schritt ihrer Schokolade &ndash; von der Bohne bis zur Tafel. Darum verwendet Gar&ccedil;oa ausschliesslich Kakaobohnen von Plantagen, die sie pers&ouml;nlich besucht haben und deren Kakaob&auml;uerinnen und &ndash;bauern sie pers&ouml;nlich kennen. So stammen die Bohnen der Gar&ccedil;oa-Schokoladen aus Chulucanas und Curiman&aacute; in Peru, Sronko in Ghana und Idukki in Indien. Bei Gar&ccedil;oa wird der Kakao lediglich mit Bio-Rohrzucker gemischt und nicht etwa mit Kakaobutter. Dadurch kann der reine Kakao-Geschmack erhalten bleiben.</p><p>Das Konzept gef&auml;llt, wie eine Auszeichnung bei den International Chocolate Awards 2018 beweist. Die Produktionsst&auml;tte von Gar&ccedil;oa ist zwar klein, trotzdem k&ouml;nnen Interessierte Schokoladen-Fans die Manufaktur im Rahmen der &laquo;Schoggisafari&raquo; besuchen und erfahren dabei, wie Gar&ccedil;oa-Tafeln entstehen.</p></p>"@de,
        "<p>The manufacturers at Gar&ccedil;oa need just two ingredients to produce their intensively flavored chocolate. That sounds simple, but it requires the very best ingredients &ndash; the purest of cacao and top-quality cane sugar &ndash; and time.<p>With the bean-to-bar movement, producers monitor every step of their chocolate production, from the cacao bean right through the final chocolate bar. As a result, Gar&ccedil;oa only uses cacao beans from plantations they have visited themselves and whose farmers they know personally. Thus the cacao beans used for Gar&ccedil;oa chocolate come from Chulucanas and Curiman&aacute; in Peru, Sronko in Ghana, and Idukki in India. At Gar&ccedil;oa, the cacao is only mixed with organic cane sugar and not with cocoa butter. This preserves the pure cacao taste.</p><p>The concept has proved successful &ndash; as underscored by an award at the International Chocolate Awards 2018. Although Gar&ccedil;oa&rsquo;s production facilities are small, chocolate lovers can visit the manufactory in the course of a &ldquo;Chocolate Safari&rdquo; and learn how Gar&ccedil;oa chocolate bars are made.</p></p>"@en,
        "<p>Les cr&eacute;ateurs/-trices de Gar&ccedil;oa n&rsquo;ont besoin que de deux ingr&eacute;dients pour produire leur chocolat intense. Cela para&icirc;t tout simple mais il leur faut les meilleurs produits&nbsp;: le cacao le plus pur, le meilleur sucre de canne et du temps.<p>Les producteurs appartenant au mouvement Bean-to-Bar surveillent toutes les &eacute;tapes de leur chocolat &ndash; de la f&egrave;ve &agrave; la tablette. La&nbsp; manufacture de Gar&ccedil;oa utilise uniquement des f&egrave;ves de cacao provenant de plantations qu&rsquo;elle a visit&eacute;es et dont elle connait personnellement les cultivateurs/-trices de cacao. Les f&egrave;ves du chocolat Gar&ccedil;oa proviennent de Chulucanas et de Curiman&aacute; au P&eacute;rou, de Sronko au Ghana et d&rsquo;Idukki en Inde. Chez Gar&ccedil;oa le cacao est m&eacute;lang&eacute; uniquement &agrave; du sucre de canne bio et sans beurre de cacao &ndash; cela permet de pr&eacute;server le pur go&ucirc;t de cacao.</p><p>La distinction obtenue lors des International Chocolate Awards 2018 prouve que le concept pla&icirc;t. Le site de production de Gar&ccedil;oa est petit, mais les amateurs peuvent visiter la manufacture dans le cadre du &laquo;&nbsp;Schoggisafari&nbsp;&raquo; (safari du chocolat) et d&eacute;couvrir comment sont produites les tablettes Gar&ccedil;oa.</p></p>"@fr,
        "<p>Bastano soltanto due ingredienti per ottenere il gustoso cioccolato di Gar&ccedil;oa. Sembra facile, ma per farlo servono quelli pi&ugrave; buoni in assoluto, vale a dire il cacao pi&ugrave; puro e lo zucchero di canna grezzo migliore. E del tempo.<p>Il movimento bean-to-bar prevede che i fabbricanti sorveglino ogni fase della produzione del loro cioccolato, dalla fava alla tavoletta. Per questo Gar&ccedil;oa utilizza solo fave di cacao di piantagioni che visita di persona e delle quali conosce personalmente i coltivatori. Le fave per il cioccolato Gar&ccedil;oa provengono da Chulucanas e Curiman&aacute; in Per&ugrave;, da Sronko in Ghana e da Idukki in India. Gar&ccedil;oa miscela il suo cacao soltanto con zucchero di canna grezzo biologico, senza usare burro di cacao. In questo modo, viene preservato il sapore puro del cacao.</p><p>L&rsquo;idea piace, come testimonia un riconoscimento agli International Chocolate Awards 2018. Lo stabilimento produttivo di Gar&ccedil;oa &egrave; piccolo, ma chi vuole pu&ograve; visitare la manifattura con il cosiddetto &ldquo;Schoggisafari&rdquo; (il safari del cioccolato), scoprendo come nascono nel tavolette Gar&ccedil;oa.</p></p>"@it ;
    schema:disambiguatingDescription "Die preisgekrönte Bean-to-Bar-Schokolade aus Zürich."@de,
        "The award-winning bean-to-bar chocolate from Zurich."@en,
        "Le chocolat Bean-to-Bar primé de Zurich."@fr,
        "Il premiato cioccolato bean-to-bar di Zurigo."@it ;
